 "_doc": "The film camera (docs/interactives_backlog.md item 2; engine: Private/Photo/LyudPhoto.cpp). The photo studios' service: handing in an exposed film and collecting the prints (photo_lab, the screen \"photo_lab\", at the studio's own darkroom behind the screen, photographer on shift; the engine takes the money and keeps the films). The hero's own developing is the screen \"photo_darkroom\" on the darkroom acts (activities.json darkroom, x_p_club3.json cog_darkroom). The camera and the films are sold at the studio's desk (counters.json shop photo, stories.json photo_desk). The album's three stamp sets are given by the game's code (\"by\": \"code\", ULyudCityThings::GiveStamp when a film is developed with a sharp frame of the subject): photo_birds = the species ids of Content/BirdsData/species.json, photo_sky = sunset_<weather regime> (ELyudWeatherRegime in snake case) and aurora, photo_life = fest_<festival id of Content/PeopleData/festivals.json>, fish, maru; a new species or festival is added here by hand. The quest city_portrait («Портрет города») is given by the photographer (topic photo.city, talk.json) and hears the event photo <map place> when a developed film has a frame taken there. Strings: strings/photo.json. The photo contest (backlog item 33; docs/photo.md): the photo club at «Шестерня» runs it by the month, the engine (Private/Photo) keeps the entries, the jury and the wall; here are its two things: the table with the box of prints (photo_contest, the screen \"photo_contest\": hand a print in on days 1..25, hear the result from the 26th; the thing P-CLUB3/contest_box is made of the stool spot photo_seat_2 by the table with the projector and the cardboard box, a \"spot\" rule) and the wall of winners (photo_wall, the screen \"photo_wall\": the hero's prize prints; the lab's end wall with the line of prints, P-CLUB3/drying_line, whose rule is in x_p_club3.json). Three photo quests from residents hear photo <target> too, where the target may be the dog (maru) or a resident's key (interiors.py photo_subjects): grandpa_portrait (the repairman Nurlan Liepa of the workshop W1-U04 wants a portrait of his grandfather Klaus Liepa, t_liepa_klaus; topic set photo_grandpa on W1-U04/repair_counter), old_pier (the lighthouse keepers want the pier before it is repainted, map place pier; topic set photo_pier on P-PIER/tower_desk, x_p_pier.json) and maru_wall (the Cog's photo circle wants Maru for its wall; topic set photo_maru on P-CLUB3/cloak, x_p_club3.json). Their photo stage is no_skip: showing a print that does not exist finishes nothing.",
